@startuml
title Adapter / Wrapper

skinparam legendBackgroundColor #f9f9f9
skinparam legendBorderColor #999999

legend right

**Intent**:
Convert one interface to another expected by clients.

**Motivation**:
Integrate legacy/third-party component with incompatible method signatures.

**Applicability**:
You have an existing implementation but incompatible interface.
Want to avoid refactoring clients or the adaptee.

**Participants**:
Target desired interface; Adaptee existing interface; Adapter translates.

**Implementation Notes**:
Class Adapter (inheritance) vs Object Adapter (composition).
Handle exception, data-type, and semantic mismatches carefully.

**Known Uses**:
Java IO decorators often act as adapters; JDBC drivers;
Collections.list(Enumeration) adapting legacy APIs.

**Related Patterns**:
Facade (simplify), Bridge (separate abstraction/implementation),
Decorator (add behavior).

endlegend

interface Target {
  +request()
}

class Adapter implements Target {
  -adaptee : Adaptee
  +request()
}

class Adaptee {
  +specificRequest()
}

class Client
Client ..> Target
Adapter o-- Adaptee
@enduml